  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the arithmetic mean of outcomes (ignoring probabilities), which in this case leads to preferring B due to its higher maximum outcome (2500 vs. 2400). The individual also prefers B and bases their choice on the higher payout if the positive outcome occurs, despite similar probabilities. While the decision reason and the individual’s justification both lead to selecting B and are influenced by the higher outcome in B, the individual does not mention or imply any calculation involving averaging outcomes. Instead, their reasoning appears to be a simple outcome comparison — choosing the lottery with the higher prize when probabilities are seen as similar. This resembles a 'satisficing' or 'priority heuristic' approach rather than computing a mean of outcomes. Therefore, although the relevant information (higher outcome in B) is considered, the specific rule of the decision reason (calculating the mean of outcomes) is not reflected in the verbal report. The justification aligns partially with the informational basis of the reason but not with its rule-based structure.",
  "final_assessment_score": 30
